#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:9
msgid "Understanding parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:11
msgid "**Goal:** Learn how to get, set, save and reload parameters in ROS 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:13
msgid "**Tutorial level:** Beginner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:15
msgid "**Time:** 5 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:19
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:22
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:24
msgid ""
"A parameter is a configuration value of a node. You can think of parameters "
"as node settings. A node can store parameters as integers, floats, booleans, "
"strings, and lists. In ROS 2, each node maintains its own parameters. For "
"more background on parameters, please see :doc:`the concept document "
"<../../../About-Parameters>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:31
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:33
msgid ""
"This tutorial uses the :doc:`turtlesim package <../../../../Get-Started/"
"Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:35
msgid ""
"As always, don't forget to source ROS 2 in :doc:`every new terminal you open "
"<../../../../Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:38
msgid "Tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:41
msgid "1 Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:43
msgid ""
"Start up the two turtlesim nodes, ``/turtlesim`` and ``/teleop_turtle``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:45
msgid "Open a new terminal and run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:47
msgid "$ ros2 run turtlesim turtlesim_node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:51
msgid "Open another terminal and run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:53
msgid "$ ros2 run turtlesim turtle_teleop_key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:59
msgid "2 ros2 param list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:61
msgid ""
"To see the parameters belonging to your nodes, open a new terminal and enter "
"the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:63
msgid ""
"$ ros2 param list\n"
"/teleop_turtle:\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.depth\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.durability\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.history\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.reliability\n"
"  scale_angular\n"
"  scale_linear\n"
"  use_sim_time\n"
"/turtlesim:\n"
"  background_b\n"
"  background_g\n"
"  background_r\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.depth\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.durability\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.history\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.reliability\n"
"  use_sim_time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:85
msgid ""
"You see the node namespaces, ``/teleop_turtle`` and ``/turtlesim``, followed "
"by each node's parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:87
msgid ""
"The namespaces of the parameter and its name are separated using dots as you "
"can see, for example, in ``parameter_events.publisher.depth``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:89
msgid ""
"Every node has the parameter ``use_sim_time``; it's not unique to turtlesim."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:91
msgid ""
"Based on their names, it looks like ``/turtlesim``'s parameters determine "
"the background color of the turtlesim window using RGB color values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:93
msgid "To determine a parameter's type, you can use ``ros2 param get``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:97
msgid "3 ros2 param get"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:99
msgid "To display the type and current value of a parameter, use the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:101
msgid "$ ros2 param get <node_name> <parameter_name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:105
msgid ""
"You can also query a parameter across all nodes by omitting the node name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:107
msgid "$ ros2 param get <parameter_name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:111
msgid ""
"Let's find out the current value of ``/turtlesim``'s parameter "
"``background_g``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:113
msgid ""
"$ ros2 param get /turtlesim background_g\n"
"Integer value is: 86"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:118
msgid "Now you know ``background_g`` holds an integer value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:120
msgid ""
"If you run the same command on ``background_r`` and ``background_b``, you "
"will get the values ``69`` and ``255``, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:122
msgid "You can also check the ``use_sim_time`` parameter across all nodes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:124
msgid "$ ros2 param get use_sim_time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:128
msgid ""
"This will display the parameter value for each node that has this parameter "
"set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:131
msgid "4 ros2 param set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:133
msgid "To change a parameter's value at runtime, use the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:135
msgid "$ ros2 param set <node_name> <parameter_name> <value>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:139
msgid "Let's change ``/turtlesim``'s background color:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:141
msgid ""
"$ ros2 param set /turtlesim background_r 150\n"
"Set parameter successful"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:146
msgid "The background of your turtlesim window should change colors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:150
msgid ""
"Setting parameters with the ``set`` command will only change them in your "
"current session, not permanently. However, you can save your settings and "
"reload them the next time you start a node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:154
msgid "5 ros2 param dump"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:156
msgid ""
"You can view all of a node's current parameter values by using the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:158
msgid "$ ros2 param dump <node_name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:162
msgid ""
"The command prints to the standard output (stdout) by default but you can "
"also redirect the parameter values into a file to save them for later. To "
"save your current configuration of ``/turtlesim``'s parameters into the file "
"``turtlesim.yaml``, enter the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:165
msgid "$ ros2 param dump /turtlesim > turtlesim.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:169
msgid ""
"You will find a new file in the current working directory your shell is "
"running in. If you open this file, you'll see the following content:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:172
msgid ""
"/turtlesim:\n"
"  ros__parameters:\n"
"    background_b: 255\n"
"    background_g: 86\n"
"    background_r: 150\n"
"    qos_overrides:\n"
"      /parameter_events:\n"
"        publisher:\n"
"          depth: 1000\n"
"          durability: volatile\n"
"          history: keep_last\n"
"          reliability: reliable\n"
"    use_sim_time: false"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:188
msgid ""
"Dumping parameters comes in handy if you want to reload the node with the "
"same parameters in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:191
msgid "6 ros2 param load"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:193
msgid ""
"You can load parameters from a file to a currently running node using the "
"command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:195
msgid "$ ros2 param load <node_name> <parameter_file>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:199
msgid ""
"To load the ``turtlesim.yaml`` file generated with ``ros2 param dump`` into "
"``/turtlesim`` node's parameters, enter the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:201
msgid ""
"$ ros2 param load /turtlesim turtlesim.yaml\n"
"Set parameter background_b successful\n"
"Set parameter background_g successful\n"
"Set parameter background_r successful\n"
"Set parameter qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.depth failed: "
"parameter 'qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.depth' cannot be set "
"because it is read-only\n"
"Set parameter qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.durability failed: "
"parameter 'qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.durability' cannot be "
"set because it is read-only\n"
"Set parameter qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.history failed: "
"parameter 'qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.history' cannot be set "
"because it is read-only\n"
"Set parameter qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.reliability failed: "
"parameter 'qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.reliability' cannot be "
"set because it is read-only\n"
"Set parameter use_sim_time successful"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:215
msgid ""
"Read-only parameters can only be modified at startup and not afterwards, "
"that is why there are some warnings for the \"qos_overrides\" parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:220
msgid "7 Load parameter file on node startup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:222
msgid "To start the same node using your saved parameter values, use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:224
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run <package_name> <executable_name> --ros-args --params-file "
"<file_name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:228
msgid ""
"This is the same command you always use to start turtlesim, with the added "
"flags ``--ros-args`` and ``--params-file``, followed by the file you want to "
"load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:230
msgid ""
"Stop your running turtlesim node, and try reloading it with your saved "
"parameters, using:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:232
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run turtlesim turtlesim_node --ros-args --params-file turtlesim.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:236
msgid ""
"The turtlesim window should appear as usual, but with the purple background "
"you set earlier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:240
msgid ""
"When a parameter file is used at node startup, all parameters, including the "
"read-only ones, will be updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:243
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:245
msgid ""
"Nodes have parameters to define their default configuration values. You can "
"``get`` and ``set`` parameter values from the command line. You can also "
"save the parameter settings to a file to reload them in a future session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:250
msgid "Next steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:252
msgid ""
"Jumping back to ROS 2 communication methods, in the next tutorial you'll "
"learn about :doc:`actions <../../../interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/"
"Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions>`."
msgstr ""
